      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> FIN silence can result from an open stack that does not reply or from a control that drops the probe. The safest reading keeps both explanations visible.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>hping3 -F -p 8080 10.42.18.73</b> and interpret the reported result.",
      "taskQuestion": "What is the safest interpretation of the FIN result?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> Correct. The FIN result remains open|filtered or a policy drop until another observation corroborates it.",
      "answers": [
        "No response here is firm proof that remote exploitation of the host is possible.",
        "No response can mean open|filtered or a policy drop; corroborate it.",
        "FIN packets are never written to any firewall log.",
        "An RST reply always means the firewall is absent."
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1
    },
